# Firebending Student: with the Student gone when its firebending ability resolves, X is its power as it last existed on the
# battlefield (CR 608.2h, 113.7a). Shock triggers prowess, so it attacks as a 2/3; with the ability on the stack Bot2 bolts it.
# The ability adds {R}{R}, its last power, not the {R} of the 1/2 card now in the graveyard.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Ruby x2
Firebending Student
Shock
Mountain x15

[Bot2 Deck]
Mox Ruby
Lightning Bolt
Mountain x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby#1.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby#2.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Firebending Student.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby#1.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Shock.Cast(Bot2)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield.Firebending Student.Power = 2
Bot1.Attack(Firebending Student > Bot2)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Firebending Student)
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
? Bot1.Graveyard = Firebending Student; Shock
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass

[Expect]
Bot1.Mana = {R}{R} lasting {R}{R}
